 {url}←StartTatinServer port;tatin;home;folder;iniFile;lines;encoding;newline;ind;parms;process;counter;maxTries;ready
⍝ Starts a Tatin test server on `port` in a process of its own and returns its URL once it answers.
⍝ Meant for looking at the web pages in a browser, like when working on the layout.
⍝ Stop it with `StopTatinServer`.
⍝ The server works on a temporary copy of TestServer/ with the port and the temp folder (which
⍝ holds the log) changed in its INI file, so neither the project's test data nor the port and the
⍝ log of the test cases' server are touched, and several servers can run side by side on
⍝ different ports. It runs the code in APLSource/ as it is on disk and serves the assets in
⍝ TestServer/Server/Assets/.
⍝ Unlike the server the test cases start, it collects no code coverage and writes no test log.
⍝ When the server does not answer, its session and its folder are left for inspection.
 tatin←##.##
 'Specify a port number, like 5099'##.Assert(1=≢port)∧(⊃port)∊⍳65535
 port←⊃port
 :If 0=⎕NC'∆SERVERS'
     ∆SERVERS←0 3⍴⍬                                   ⍝ Port, process and folder of every server started
 :EndIf
 ('A server started earlier runs on port ',⍕port)##.Assert~port∊∆SERVERS[;1]
 url←'https://localhost:',(⍕port),'/'
 :If 0=tatin.Client.⎕NC'R'
     tatin.Admin.Initialize_Client
 :EndIf
 ('Something answers on port ',(⍕port),' already')##.Assert~1 tatin.Client.Ping url
 home←tatin.CiderConfig.HOME
 folder←tatin.FilesAndDirs.GetTempSubDir'Tatin-Server-',⍕port
 (folder,'/')⎕NCOPY⍠('Wildcard' 1)⊣home,'/TestServer/*'
 iniFile←folder,'/Server/server.ini'
 (lines encoding newline)←⎕NGET iniFile 1
 ind←{'Port='≡(≢'Port=')↑⍵}¨lines                  ⍝ The first one is in [CONFIG]; [EMAIL] has one as well
 ('No "Port=" in ',iniFile)##.Assert∨/ind
 lines[ind⍳1]←⊂'Port=',⍕port
⍝ "temp" holds the log folder, among other things; the INI file puts it into a fixed folder shared
⍝ by all test servers, so it must point into this server's own folder
 ind←{'temp='≡(≢'temp=')↑⍵}¨lines
 ('No "temp=" in ',iniFile)##.Assert∨/ind
 lines[ind⍳1]←⊂'temp=''',folder,'/Temp/'''
 3 ⎕MKDIR folder,'/Temp/Logs'
 (lines encoding newline)⎕NPUT iniFile 1
 parms←tatin.APLProcess.CreateParms
 parms.Exe←##.GetAPLVersion''
 parms.ConfigParms⍪←'load'(home,'/APLSource/Admin/TestServer/RunTatinServer.aplf')
 parms.ConfigParms⍪←'lx' '#.RunTatinServer 1'
 parms.ConfigParms⍪←'tatinHome'home
 parms.ConfigParms⍪←'serverPath'folder
 parms.SessionFile←1
 parms.WindowsStyle←'Normal'
 parms.Wait←0
 process←tatin.APLProcess.New parms
 maxTries←120                                         ⍝ Half a second each
 counter←0
 :Repeat
     ⎕DL 0.5
     counter+←1
     ready←1 tatin.Client.Ping url
 :Until ready∨process.HasExited∨maxTries<counter
 :If ready
     ∆SERVERS⍪←port process folder
     ⎕←'Tatin server running at ',url
 :Else
⍝ Session and folder are left alone: they are what is needed to find out what went wrong.
⍝ A session still running is registered, so that `StopTatinServer` can deal with it later.
     :If ~process.HasExited
         ∆SERVERS⍪←port process folder
     :EndIf
     ('The server on port ',(⍕port),' did not answer; see its session window for why. Its folder: ',folder)##.Assert 0
 :EndIf
⍝Done
